This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Two of the rule's three shapes apply, either alone being sufficient.

Its SUBJECT is scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh, which is not installed: install.sh's
copy loop derives from core/fixtures/ and core/scripts/, and never touches the repo-root
scripts/. Its CORPUS is docs/backlog.md, this repository's own carry-over backlog, and a
consumer tree gets no docs/backlog.md at all. On a consumer this fixture would resolve no
validator and no ledger, and could only pass -- a unit that cannot fail scores as a pass in
the consumer's own suite verdict.

It also copies scripts/backlog-reverify.sh into every seed, which does not exist on a consumer.
Its receipt join (rj) moved to core/fixtures/backlog-receipt-fixture-join/ under BL-918. Its real-ledger population join (j1) moved
to core/fixtures/backlog-real-ledger/, which runs it over a frozen ledger snapshot; against the
live docs/backlog.md it runs as arm R9 of scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh at pre-push.

The consumer's equivalent ledger is the push-candidate ledger under
_bmad-output/ai-dlc-update/, whose own fixtures (ledger-reverify, ledger-rotate,
ledger-status-vocabulary, ledger-reverify-unfalsifiable) ship and cover it. This one must not
be confused for those, and its siblings core/fixtures/backlog-size-ceiling/,
core/fixtures/backlog-real-ledger/, core/fixtures/backlog-ledger/ and core/fixtures/backlog-rotate-fence-guard/ carry the same
declaration for the same reason.
